\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f0\fs22 1\plain \f0\super\fs28 r\plain \f0\fs22 -16\plain \f0\super\fs28 r\plain \f0\fs22  {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[0].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f0\scaps\fs22\chcbpat17 [Pseudo-]Apuleius [Madaurensis}}\plain \f0\scaps\fs22 :] {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[0].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f0\scaps\fs22\chcbpat17 Asclepius}}\plain \f0\scaps\fs22 .\plain \f0\fs22  Mit Prolog: {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[1].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f0\scaps\fs22\chcbpat17 Aurelius Augustinus}}\plain \f0\scaps\fs22 : {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[1].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f0\scaps\fs22\chcbpat17 Tractatus [adversus quinque haereses}}{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[1].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f0\fs22\chcbpat17 , Auszug (Prologus super librum Trimegisti ad Asclepium)}}\plain \f0\fs22 ]. \plain \f0\i\fs22 >Incipit Prologus beati Augustini super librum Trimegisti ad Asclepium<. {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[0].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f0\i\fs22\chcbpat17 Augustinus libro contra quinque hereses: Hermes, qui appellatur latine Mercurius scripsit librum, qui Logostileos }}{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[0].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f0\fs22\chcbpat17 (!) }}{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[0].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f0\i\fs22\chcbpat17 dicitur}}\plain \f0\i\fs22  ... - ... que in serie libri commemorabimus.\plain \f0\fs22  Ed.: {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezlit[0].8330/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f0\fs22\chcbpat17 PL}}\plain \f0\fs22 , Bd. 42, Sp. 1102f. (stark gek\u252 \'fcrzt). (1\plain \f0\super\fs28 r\plain \f0\fs22 ) Text: \plain \f0\i\fs22 >Hermis Trimegisti helera \plain \f0\fs22 (!) \plain \f0\i\fs22 ad Asclepium allocuta incipit feliciter. Trimestistus. Capitulum primum<. Asclepius iste pro sole michi est. {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[1].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f0\i\fs22\chcbpat17 Deus, deus te nobis, o Asclepi, ut divino sermone (!) interesses adduxit}}\plain \f0\i\fs22  ... - ... ad puram et sine animalibus cenam.\plain \f0\fs22  Danach Subscriptio (fehlerhaft): \plain \f0\i\fs22 \u919 ?\u951 ?\u961 ?\u956 \'b5\u959 ?\u953 ? T\u959 ?\u953 ?\u956 \'b5\u951 ?\u915 G\u953 ?s\u964 t\u959 ?\u953 ? \plain \f0\fs22 (!) \plain \f0\i\fs22 biba \plain \f0\fs22 (!) \plain \f0\i\fs22 osi\u951 ?\u961 ?a \u960 p\u961 ?\u959 ?s aska\u951 ? \plain \f0\fs22 (!) \plain \f0\i\fs22 \u960 p\u961 ?os\u966 fo\u951 ?\u951 ?\u966 f\u951 ?sa\plain \f0\fs22  (!)\plain \f0\i\fs22 .\plain \f0\fs22  Ed.: Walter Scott (Hg.): Hermetica. The ancient Greek and Latin writings which contain religious or philosophic teachings ascribed to Hermes Trismegistos, Bd. 1. Oxford 1924 (ND Boston/Mass. 1985), S. 286-376. Am Rand zahlreiche Glossen von Schreiberhand, lat., einmal auch griech. (5\plain \f0\super\fs28 v\plain \f0\fs22 ). 16\plain \f0\super\fs28 v\plain \f0\fs22 -17\plain \f0\super\fs28 r\plain \f0\fs22  leer.}

