\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f0\fs22 1\plain \f0\super\fs28 ra\plain \f0\fs22 -247\plain \f0\super\fs28 ra\plain \f0\fs22  {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[0].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f0\scaps\fs22\chcbpat17 Raimundus de Sabunde}}\plain \f0\scaps\fs22 : {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[0].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f0\scaps\fs22\chcbpat17 [Theologia naturalis sive] Liber creaturarum}}\plain \f0\scaps\fs22 .\plain \f0\fs22  Prolog: \plain \f0\i\fs22 >{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[0].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f0\i\fs22\chcbpat17 In alpha sit principium et in o finis meus, qui est Christus dominus noster. Incipit Liber nature sive creaturarum ... compositus a venerabili viro magistro Reymundo }}{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[0].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f0\fs22\chcbpat17 (korr. }}{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[0].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f0\i\fs22\chcbpat17 Raymundo}}{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[0].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f0\fs22\chcbpat17 ) }}{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[0].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f0\i\fs22\chcbpat17 Sabunde}}{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[0].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f0\fs22\chcbpat17  (korr. }}{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[0].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f0\i\fs22\chcbpat17 Sabaudie}}{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[0].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f0\fs22\chcbpat17 )}}\plain \f0\fs22  \plain \f0\i\fs22 ...<. {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[1].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f0\i\fs22\chcbpat17 Ad laudem et gloriam altissime et gloriosissime trinitatis sanctissimeque Dei genitricis virginis Marie et tocius curie celestis}}\plain \f0\i\fs22  ... \plain \f0\fs22 (2\plain \f0\super\fs28 va\plain \f0\fs22 ) Text: {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[2].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f0\i\fs22\chcbpat17 Quia homo naturaliter semper querit certitudinem et evidenciam claram}}\plain \f0\i\fs22  ... - ... gaudia infinita et inexcogitabilia in eternum. Ad que \plain \f0\fs22 (korr. aus \plain \f0\i\fs22 quem\plain \f0\fs22 ) \plain \f0\i\fs22 dignetur nos perducere Jesus Christus, filius Dei, rex eterne glorie, qui est benedictus in secula seculorum. Et sic est finis Libri creaturarum seu nature scilicet de homine, propter quem alie creature facte sunt. Et finitus per manus Judoci de Geldonia coadiuvante manu omnipotentis, cui sit laus et gloria nunc et in eternum. Anno domini M\plain \f0\i\super\fs28 o\plain \f0\i\fs22 cccc\plain \f0\i\super\fs28 o\plain \f0\i\fs22 lix. mensis Aprilis\plain \f0\fs22  [April 1459]\plain \f0\i\fs22 . \plain \f0\fs22 Ed.: Joachim Sighart (Hg.): Raimundi de Sabunde Theologia naturalis sive liber creaturarum. Sulzbach 1852, S. 1-626 (ohne Prolog). Am Rand sowie im Text zahlreiche Korrekturen, Nachtr\u228 \'e4ge und vereinzelte Glossen, teilweise auch mit Bleistift, mehrere H\u228 \'e4nde, letztes Dr. 15. Jh. und Anf. 16. Jh. Prolog (1\plain \f0\super\fs28 ra\plain \f0\fs22 -2\plain \f0\super\fs28 va\plain \f0\fs22 ) mit Verweis auf den Tridentiner Index gestrichen, 2. H. 16. Jh. 247\plain \f0\super\fs28 rb\plain \f0\fs22  und 247\plain \f0\super\fs28 v\plain \f0\fs22  bis auf Schriftspiegellinierung leer. 248\plain \f0\super\fs28 rv\plain \f0\fs22  leer.}

