\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f0\fs22 1\plain \f0\super\fs28 ra\plain \f0\fs22 -136\plain \f0\super\fs28 va\plain \f0\fs22  {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[1].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f0\scaps\fs22\chcbpat17 [Pseudo-]Humbertus [de Romanis}}\plain \f0\scaps\fs22  ({\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[0].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f0\scaps\fs22\chcbpat17 Guilelmus Peraldus}}\plain \f0\scaps\fs22 )\plain \f0\scaps\fs22 ]: {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[0].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f0\scaps\fs22\chcbpat17 De eruditione religiosorum}}\plain \f0\fs22 . \plain \f0\i\fs22 >Humbertus de eruditione religiosorum feliciter incipit<. \plain \f0\fs22 Als Schreibproben von der Hand des Hinricus Isernloen vorgeschaltet Ps 8,1; Ier 6,8: {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezlit[1].8330/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f0\fs22\chcbpat17 AH}}\plain \f0\fs22 , Bd. 50, Nr. 144,1-2; Nr. 143,1 (Ausz\u252 \'fcge, teilweise Abbruch mitten im Wort); danach Besitzvermerk (s.o.) sowie Verzeichnis von Leben und Werk der im Codex enthaltenen Verfasser (s.u.) vom Rubrikator. (1\plain \f0\super\fs28 v\plain \f0\fs22 ) leer. (2\plain \f0\super\fs28 ra\plain \f0\fs22 ) \plain \f0\i\fs22 >Incipit prologus venerabilis atque devotissimi viri fratris Humberti generalis magistri ... in librum, qui dicitur De eruditione religiosorum<.\plain \f0\fs22  Prolog: {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[0].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f0\i\fs22\chcbpat17 Erudire Jerusalem ... }}{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[0].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f0\fs22\chcbpat17 (Ier 6,8)}}{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[0].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f0\i\fs22\chcbpat17 . Jherusalem secundum nominis interpretacionem, que est pacifica}}\plain \f0\i\fs22  ... \plain \f0\fs22 (6\plain \f0\super\fs28 va\plain \f0\fs22 ) Text: {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[1].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f0\i\fs22\chcbpat17 Qui graciam acceptam non agnoscit de ea gracias non agit}}\plain \f0\i\fs22  ... - ... gloriosa dicta sunt de te, civitas Dei etc. Cui honor et gloria in secula seculorum. Amen. >Explicit et finit. Finitus est tractatus iste De eruditione religiosorum \plain \f0\fs22 (eingef\u252 \'fcgt \plain \f0\i\fs22 in die Lucie virginis\plain \f0\fs22 )\plain \f0\i\fs22  priore Wilhelmi Embricae preexistente \plain \f0\fs22 [Wilhelm von der Molen\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 , gen. Emmerich, Prior in Dalheim 1491\endash 1504, vgl. West\-f\u228 \'e4lisches Klosterbuch, Bd. 1, S.\~232; Kock, Hss. Dalheim, S. 330, Anm. 46\plain \f0\fs22 ] \plain \f0\i\fs22 per Hinricum fratrem Isernloen privatis fere temporibus elaboratus. Anno domini 1498 dyaconatus sub officio insignitus<. Oretis pro eo.\plain \f0\fs22  Ed.: Maguerin de la Bigne: Maxima bibliotheca veterum patrum et antiquorum scriptorum ecclesiasticorum, Bd. 25. Lyon 1677, S. 665-753. Zu Verfasser, Werk und \u220 \'dcberlieferung vgl. {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezlit[0].8330/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f0\fs22\chcbpat17 Kaeppeli, ScriptOP, 1970}}\plain \f0\fs22 , Nr. 1625; Antoine Dondaine: Guillaume Peyraut. Vie et oeuvres. In: Archivum Fratrum Praedicatorum 18 (1948), S. 215-220 (Hs jeweils genannt). Am Rand vereinzelt Korrekturen, eine Hand, Anf. 16. Jh.}

{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg0\uc1\deff0\deflang0\deflangfe0{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset1 Arial;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset1 Arial Narrow;}}{\colortbl;\red0\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;\red0\green255\blue255;\red0\green255\blue0;\red255\green0\blue255;\red255\green0\blue0;\red255\green255\blue0;\red255\green255\blue255;\red0\green0\blue128;\red0\green128\blue128;\red0\green128\blue0;\red128\green0\blue128;\red128\green0\blue0;\red128\green128\blue0;\red128\green128\blue128;\red192\green192\blue192;\red204\green238\blue221;}

