\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f0\fs22 205\plain \f0\super\fs28 r\plain \f0\fs22 -211\plain \f0\super\fs28 r\plain \f0\fs22  \plain \f0\scaps\fs22 [{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[0].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f0\scaps\fs22\chcbpat17 Etymachia}}\plain \f0\scaps\fs22 ]\plain \f0\fs22 . Fragment. \plain \f0\i\fs22 In nomine domini. Amen. >{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[0].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f0\i\fs22\chcbpat17 Misit rex Saul apparitores, ut caperent David< }}{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[0].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f0\fs22\chcbpat17 (I Sm 19,14)}}{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[0].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f0\i\fs22\chcbpat17 . Qui interpretatur desiderabilis, significat peccatorem, cuius conversionem}}\plain \f0\i\fs22  ... - ... ut consequaris eternam.\plain \f0\fs22  || Text bricht ab. Ed.: Nigel Harris: The Latin and German 'Etymachia'. Textual History, Edition, Commentary. T\u252 \'fcbingen 1994 (MTU 102), S. 108-152. Zu Verfasser, Werk und \u220 \'dcberlieferung vgl. ebd., S. 22-64; {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezlit[0].8330/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f0\fs22\chcbpat17 Bloomfield/Guyot, Incipits, 1979}}\plain \f0\fs22 , Nr. 3085 (Suppl.); {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezlit[1].8330/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f0\fs22\chcbpat17 VL (2)}}\plain \f0\fs22 , Bd. 2, Sp. 636-639. Am Rand vereinzelt Glossen und Erg\u228 \'e4nzungen von Schreiberhand. 211\plain \f0\super\fs28 v\plain \f0\fs22 -220\plain \f0\super\fs28 v\plain \f0\fs22  leer. Handwechsel.}

