\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f0\fs22 21\plain \f0\super\fs28 ra\plain \f0\fs22 -76\plain \f0\super\fs28 vb\plain \f0\fs22  {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[0].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f0\scaps\fs22\chcbpat17 Antonius Guainerius}}\plain \f0\scaps\fs22 : {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[0].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f0\scaps\fs22\chcbpat17 Summarium de febribus}}\plain \f0\scaps\fs22 . \plain \f0\fs22 Titel: \plain \f0\i\fs22 >Incipit Summarium de febribus editum per me Anthonium de Gayneriis ad insignem arcium et medicine doctorem magistrum Anthonium Maglianum de Cherio, illustrissimum domini domini ducis Subaudie \plain \f0\fs22 (!) \plain \f0\i\fs22 phisicum, ad laudem Dei patris et filii et spiritus sancti<. \plain \f0\fs22 (21\plain \f0\super\fs28 ra\plain \f0\fs22 ) Prolog: {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[0].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f0\i\fs22\chcbpat17 Tui amoris gracia, mi Anthoni Magliane, ad hunc deveni locum omnique}}\plain \f0\i\fs22  ... \plain \f0\fs22 (20\plain \f0\super\fs28 vb\plain \f0\fs22 -21\plain \f0\super\fs28 va\plain \f0\fs22 ) Inhaltsverzeichnis. (21\plain \f0\super\fs28 vb\plain \f0\fs22 ) Text: {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[1].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f0\i\fs22\chcbpat17 Cum mee sit intencionis hoc in summario febrium}}\plain \f0\i\fs22  ... - ... huic summario finem imponit, pro quo Jhesu crucifixo sint infinite laudes. Amen. Et sic est finis tractatus de febribus ... editus per Anthonium de Gayneriis de Papia in villa Cambraraci \plain \f0\fs22 (korrigiert \plain \f0\i\fs22 Crambraraci\plain \f0\fs22 )\plain \f0\i\fs22  commotantem.\plain \f0\fs22  Zu Werk und \u220 \'dcberlieferung vgl. {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezlit[0].8330/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f0\fs22\chcbpat17 Thorndike/Kibre, Catalogue of Incipits, 1963}}\plain \f0\fs22 , Sp. 1213; 1592 (Prolog); 318 (Text); BAMAT, Bd. 7, Nr. 375. Am Rand vereinzelt Glossen von Schreiberhand sowie einer weiteren Hand, Humanistica, letztes Dr. 15. Jh. (Philippus Schoen?). }

